    "biography": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Cockroaches were a common pest in pre-War America, and after the bombs fell and brought about a nuclear apocalypse, not much changed. Dubbed as radroaches for their radioactive bite, these creatures are far larger than their ancestors but are still as much of a pest. Often infesting ruined buildings, rubbish heaps, and other dark, dank locations, they attack their prey by jumping at them and attacking with their pincers. While easy to deal with in small numbers, swarms can easily overwhelm the unprepared and devastate settlements if left unchecked.</span></p>",
